    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d925">

                <pb facs="0825" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 124.55/10</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Langhorne</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-20T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 20, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>444. Your 760, March 10, 11 a.m. Is communication with Whitlock cut off both by mail and telegraph? If so, when will it
                    be reestablished? Can you explain statement that he has no funds? Keep
                    Department fully informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
